  "title": "fix round 1: T-1399 write the six acceptance tests in tests/test_gate_timeout.py",
  "spec": "Gate held T-1399 (commit b5c26d0 on wt/T-1399) as gate_red for one reason only: the six acceptance tests named below do not exist in tests/test_gate_timeout.py (acceptance gate says \"test not defined\" for each). The wiring in daemon.py, merge.py, failures.py, planner_runs.py and the migrated seams in test_daemon.py / test_merge.py are fine; the full suite was green (tests-green OK 1532). Do not rework them unless a new test exposes a bug.\n\nWrite these six tests as plain module-level functions (def test_...) or methods on the existing GateTimeoutTest class in tests/test_gate_timeout.py, using tests/_harness.py for a sandboxed ORCH_ROOT, a real sleeping shell script for the gate, and a tiny [gate] timeout_s (e.g. 1) with kill_grace_s small, so each test runs in a few seconds:\n1. test_daemon_gate_timeout_holds_as_infra_failure: a done execute task with a worktree; merge.TESTS_GREEN patched to a script that sleeps 30; pool.cfg[\"gate\"][\"timeout_s\"]=1; run daemon.gate(pool). Assert status held, hold_reason gate_timeout, pipeline.infra_failure == \"gate_timeout\", pipeline.gate_reds unchanged (absent or 0), pipeline.gate_timeouts == 2 (attempted twice).\n2. test_gate_timeout_files_no_fix_round: on that held task, daemon.auto_fix_round(pool) creates no new task and calls neither the runner probe nor the rerun (patch failures.subprocess.run and failures.gate.run_bounded to fail the test if called); planner_runs.build_ctx for it yields infra_failure_kind == \"gate_timeout\"; decision.route with that ctx returns route \"none\".\n3. test_gate_timeout_ctx_wins_over_cooling_account: same task, but the pool's account/executor named in task.account or assigned_to is cooling (set its hold so source.cooling() is truthy); build_ctx still yields infra_failure_kind == \"gate_timeout\".\n4. test_merge_path_honours_timeout: a real git repo with a target branch and a task branch (mirror the setup in tests/test_merge.py); merge.TESTS_GREEN patched to a sleeping script; [gate] timeout_s tiny via pool config in the sandbox; merge.merge returns {\"status\": \"gate_timeout\", ...}; the target branch sha before == after; task held with hold_reason gate_timeout and pipeline.infra_failure == \"gate_timeout\".\n5. test_flaky_rerun_kills_tree_on_timeout: failures.failure_kind on a held gate_red task whose flaky rerun command is a script that spawns a child `sleep 60` (write a marker file with the child's pid), with rerun_timeout=1 and the pytest probe patched to return non-zero (fallback command) or the command patched to the script; assert the classification is \"code_defect\", resume_hint.flaky_runs[0].timed_out is True, and the child pid is gone after the call (os.kill(pid, 0) raises ProcessLookupError, allowing a short wait).\n6. test_daemon_fast_red_gate_unchanged: merge.TESTS_GREEN patched to `exit 1` immediately; daemon.gate holds gate_red, pipeline.gate_reds == 1, no pipeline.infra_failure key.\n\nKeep the existing GateTimeoutTest tests. Run `uv run python -m pytest tests/test_gate_timeout.py -q` then .claude/hooks/tests-green.sh with stdin from /dev/null; commit on the task branch.",
